    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and both of its cases pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` derived field on the owner response so it returns `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` property (string enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time, producing `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that sets `contactPreference` to `EMAIL` when the owner has a non-blank email, else `PHONE`. This mirrors the existing derived-field style already used for `membershipLevel`, `displayName`, etc.\n\nThe rule is evaluated at response-mapping time (like the other derived fields), so it works for both `GET /api/owners/{id}` and the create response. Verified: `corePhoneWhenNoEmail` \u2192 `PHONE`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent` \u2192 `EMAIL`, both passing (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
